zzz/machine-runs — OUTPUTS OF RUNS OF THE MACHINE, KEPT AS PROVENANCE.

WHAT THESE ARE.  Files a run of interactive/ WROTE, which a checked module
then cites because the module's content came out of that run.  The theorem
is the Agda; this is the evidence that a machine, not a person, named it.
They sit under zzz/ with the rest of the archive, and unlike the rest of
zzz/ they are LOAD-BEARING: nine live citations from formal/ point here.

WHY THEY ARE TRACKED.  A citation to a file no clone carries is not a
citation.  Each line below is a live claim: the module says the file says
something, and the file is here to be read.  They were briefly untracked on
2026-08-25 as lane-era data and put back the same day, because reading the
citations showed they are not session state — they are what the run found.

